1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,590
Hey techies! Sneha here

2
00:00:02,590 --> 00:00:04,419
from Zillenial Talk.

3
00:00:04,419 --> 00:00:06,335
Season 1, episode 15.

4
00:00:06,635 --> 00:00:07,946
Quick question: does AI

5
00:00:07,946 --> 00:00:08,984
read words the way

6
00:00:08,984 --> 00:00:09,421
you do?

7
00:00:09,721 --> 00:00:12,038
Not quite. It reads tokens.

8
00:00:12,688 --> 00:00:13,724
Imagine your sentence

9
00:00:13,724 --> 00:00:14,572
is a LEGO castle.

10
00:00:14,872 --> 00:00:15,865
Before AI can use

11
00:00:15,865 --> 00:00:16,969
it, the castle gets

12
00:00:16,969 --> 00:00:18,680
taken apart into small bricks.

13
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:20,467
Those bricks are called tokens.

14
00:00:21,117 --> 00:00:22,000
A token can be

15
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:22,824
a whole word,

16
00:00:22,824 --> 00:00:23,766
part of a word,

17
00:00:23,766 --> 00:00:25,002
or even punctuation.

18
00:00:25,302 --> 00:00:26,656
Common words are often

19
00:00:26,656 --> 00:00:27,598
one token. Rare

20
00:00:27,598 --> 00:00:28,892
or long words usually

21
00:00:28,892 --> 00:00:29,540
get split.

22
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:30,435
So a token

23
00:00:30,435 --> 00:00:31,246
is not exactly

24
00:00:31,246 --> 00:00:31,679
a word.

25
00:00:32,329 --> 00:00:34,086
Why care? Because tokens

26
00:00:34,086 --> 00:00:35,001
get counted.

27
00:00:35,301 --> 00:00:36,533
AI can only handle

28
00:00:36,533 --> 00:00:37,636
so many at once.

29
00:00:37,636 --> 00:00:38,349
That limit

30
00:00:38,349 --> 00:00:39,841
is the context window,

31
00:00:39,841 --> 00:00:40,879
coming up next.

32
00:00:41,179 --> 00:00:42,459
Many AI services also

33
00:00:42,459 --> 00:00:43,681
charge by the token,

34
00:00:43,681 --> 00:00:44,903
and more tokens take

35
00:00:44,903 --> 00:00:45,543
more time.

36
00:00:46,193 --> 00:00:47,290
Where the LEGO idea

37
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:48,826
breaks: tokens aren't neat,

38
00:00:48,826 --> 00:00:50,363
equal bricks, and different

39
00:00:50,363 --> 00:00:52,063
models split text differently.

40
00:00:52,713 --> 00:00:53,415
So, a token

41
00:00:53,415 --> 00:00:54,408
is a small piece

42
00:00:54,408 --> 00:00:55,343
of text that AI

43
00:00:55,343 --> 00:00:56,394
reads and writes.

44
00:00:56,694 --> 00:00:58,393
Next up: the context

45
00:00:58,393 --> 00:01:00,577
window, the AI's suitcase.

46
00:01:00,877 --> 00:01:02,222
One tech concept.

47
00:01:02,222 --> 00:01:03,566
One simple story.

48
00:01:03,566 --> 00:01:05,060
I'm Sneha, and this

49
00:01:05,060 --> 00:01:06,479
is Zillenial Talk.

